## 6. Manual checklist (UI quality — `ui-quality.md`)

For any UI feature, walk every state (force them; don't assume):
- [ ] Loading / empty / error / success-toast states
- [ ] Affordances visible without hover; no dead controls
- [ ] Create & edit share one component (feature parity)
- [ ] Round-trip fidelity (save → reload → re-edit unchanged)
- [ ] Data refreshes after mutation (Angular HttpClient services cache tags)
- [ ] Keyboard + focus + WCAG AA contrast
- [ ] Verified in a browser (screenshots attached)

## 7. Entry / exit for this feature

**Entry** (ready for QA — `QA-PROCESS.md §5`): deployed to QA env · `/test` green ·
merged Mongoose contract · acceptance criteria linked · known limitations stated.

**Exit — feature certified (Definition of Done, `QA-PROCESS.md §5b`):** every AC case ✅ ·
no open S1/S2 · automated cases in the `qa-suite`/e2e run · gaps accepted or ticketed ·
verified on the deployed build. On certification: set `status: Certified <version>`, add
`qa:verified` + a certification comment on the feature issue, and refresh the traceability index.

